PixelU-Wii: copyright and licences
===================================

PixelU-Wii (PixelU\wii\PixelU-Wii.exe) is RetroPixels' GameCube and Wii
engine. This file says who owns which parts of it and under which terms each
part is shipped. The licence texts are in the Licenses folder next to this
file.


1. RetroPixels' own code and art
--------------------------------

Every source file of the program starts with the line

    Original code for RetroPixels (PixelU-Wii). Not derived from Dolphin.

(the one exception is listed in section 3). They were written for
RetroPixels and are RetroPixels' work, as are its build files. So are the
program icon, the pictures in Sys\Resources (except the font files), the icon
theme Sys\Themes\PixelU, all drawn by pixelu/wii/art/make_art.py, and the
rest of PixelU-Wii's own Sys data in pixelu/wii/Data/Sys: the shaders in
Sys\Shaders, the controller profiles in Sys\Profiles, the WiiConnect24
defaults in Sys\Wii (made by pixelu/wii/Data/make_wc24.py) and
Sys\ApprovedInis.json. The GameCube fonts Sys\GC\font_western.bin and
font_japanese.bin are drawn by pixelu/wii/Data/make_ipl_fonts.py from Noto
Sans and Noto Sans JP and are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, as those
fonts are (Sys\GC\font-licenses.txt).

No licence has been chosen for RetroPixels' own code yet. This notice does
not grant one and does not choose one: all rights are reserved.

How it came to be: PixelU-Wii started as a fork of the Dolphin
emulator (https://dolphin-emu.org/, GPL-2.0-or-later). Every Dolphin source
file, build file and data file has since been replaced. The replacements
were written by people who had read Dolphin's code, so this was not a
"clean room" rewrite; the repository's tools/verbatim-audit.py checks that
no Dolphin code was copied. PixelU-Wii and RetroPixels are not affiliated
with the Dolphin project.

The program has no GUI toolkit: its game window and hotkeys are its own
code (Source/Core/DolphinNoGUI). It is not linked with any GPL or LGPL
library.


2. Sys data that is not RetroPixels' own
----------------------------------------

These come from other projects:

  Sys\wiitdb-*.txt,          game title lists from GameTDB
   Sys\triforcetdb-*.txt     (https://www.gametdb.com/), credit to GameTDB
                             and its contributors
  Sys\codehandler.bin        Gecko code handler, Copyright (c) 2010-2017
                             Nuke, brkirch, Y.S, Kenobi, gamemasterplc,
                             based on Gecko OS's code handler; MIT licence
                             (Licenses\MIT.txt)
  Sys\Resources\OSD_Font.ttf Bitstream Vera Sans Mono (section 3)

Everything else in Sys is RetroPixels' own (section 1).


3. Third-party components
-------------------------

PixelU-Wii includes or links the following projects. Each keeps its own
licence and copyright. The standard licence texts are in Licenses\; each
project's own licence file, with its copyright lines, is copied at build
time into Licenses\Externals\<project>\. None of them is under the GPL or
the LGPL.

  Component                            Licence (Licenses\...)
  -----------------------------------  ----------------------------------------
  SDL 3                                Zlib
  SFML (network)                       Zlib
  zlib-ng                              Zlib
  minizip-ng                           Zlib
  ed25519 (Orson Peters)               Zlib
  libspng                              BSD-2-Clause
  LZ4                                  BSD-2-Clause
  xxHash                               BSD-2-Clause
  picojson                             BSD-2-Clause
  Zstandard                            BSD-3-Clause (its other choice, GPL-2.0,
                                       is not used)
  MiniUPnPc                            BSD-3-Clause
  hidapi                               BSD-3-Clause (one of its licence choices)
  FatFs (ChaN)                         FatFs licence (BSD-1-Clause style;
                                       Licenses\Externals\FatFs)
  cubeb                                ISC
  mbed TLS                             Apache-2.0
  SPIRV-Cross                          Apache-2.0
  glslang                              BSD-3-Clause, MIT and Apache-2.0 parts
  Vulkan-Headers                       Apache-2.0 / MIT
  VulkanMemoryAllocator                MIT
  Dear ImGui, ImPlot                   MIT
  fmt                                  MIT
  ENet                                 MIT
  pugixml                              MIT
  tinygltf                             MIT
  watcher                              MIT
  cpp-ipc                              MIT
  cpp-optparse                         MIT
  discord-rpc, RapidJSON               MIT
  expr                                 MIT
  rcheevos                             MIT
  Windows Implementation Libraries     MIT
  Khronos OpenGL extension headers     MIT (Source/Core/Common/GL/GLExtensions,
                                       Copyright The Khronos Group Inc.; the
                                       one part of Source/ that is not
                                       RetroPixels' own)
  curl                                 curl licence
  bzip2                                bzip2-1.0.6
  liblzma (XZ Utils)                   0BSD / public domain
  mGBA                                 MPL-2.0 (file-level copyleft: changes to
                                       mGBA's own files would be shared under
                                       MPL-2.0; none are made)
  Bitstream Vera Sans Mono             Bitstream-Vera (Sys\Resources\
   (Sys\Resources\OSD_Font.ttf)         OSD_Font_VeraMono_Copyright.txt)
  Microsoft Visual C++ runtime DLLs    Microsoft's redistribution terms (Visual
                                       Studio redistributable files)

Every third-party source is fetched from its own project
(pixelu/wii/Externals/sources.json); expr, which has no upstream for the
version used, is kept in pixelu/wii/Externals.

"GameCube" and "Wii" are trademarks of Nintendo. PixelU-Wii and RetroPixels
are not affiliated with Nintendo. No Nintendo keys, firmware, BIOS/IPL
images, DSP ROMs or games are included.
